  "worked_solution": "The set $D\u2216C$ is the set of all elements belonging to $D$ but *not* $C.$ Note that the elements $4,8,12,24\\in C$ are also in $D,$ so we must remove them. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D\u2216C & =D-C \\\\  & ={0,4,8,12,16,20,24}-{1,2,3,4,8,12,24} \\\\  & ={0,16,20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
